From 73627dc7f9f42daf9e302b4e3436447bda525609 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:37:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] sycl: XMX small-batch mat-mul for Q3_K and IQ3_S; the
 fewest columns per type

Extend the XMX mat-mul to Q3_K, read in its reorder layout (a 3-bit code is 2 bits of qs and
1 of hmask; code | 0x6400 is fp16 1024 + code, less 1028), and to IQ3_S, read in its plain
110-byte blocks (only 2-byte aligned, so loaded 16 bits at a time): each 4 values are one of
512 grid entries, kept in shared memory as fp16 pairs in operand order, with the signs applied
by an xor on the sign bits.

The fewest columns the path takes now depends on the type: 1 for IQ3_S, whose dp4a kernel runs
at a fifth of the read rate even at one column; 2 for Q3_K, whose multi-column dp4a kernel
already costs 3x its single column at 2; 1 for IQ4_XS in its reorder layout, as before; 4 for
the rest. The per-type lookup table is now sized by the block type.

Arc Pro B70, test-backend-ops perf, dp4a -> XMX, us at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 columns:
  Q3_K   17408x5120  108 / 321 / 366 / 483 -> (dp4a) / 123 / 123 / 125
  Q3_K   5120x17408  104 / 346 / 391 / 514 -> (dp4a) / 105 / 107 / 113
  IQ3_S  5120x17408  329 / 660 / 1314 / 2648 -> 250 / 252 / 253 / 254
  IQ3_S  17408x5120  308 / 614 / 1216 / 2463 -> 269 / 266 / 267 / 268
test-backend-ops MUL_MAT, MUL_MAT_VEC_FUSION and reorder-then-batch pass against the CPU; the
XMX eval cases cover all six types from 1 to 8 tokens.
